sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-anchiornis-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-anchiornis-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-anchiornis-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Anchiornis huxleyi Turing wavenumber at 2.0 nm (Late Jurassic, 160.0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 83.9/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Schnakenberg reaction-diffusion with slot-3111 parameters a=0.062, b=1.28, Du=0.72, Dv=31.5. Analytical lambda_c is calibrated to 2.0 nm (2.0e-9 m, log10=-8.699) at 160.0 Ma. Trace is negative, det=(a+b)^2>0, k_c=0.776 sits inside the unstable band, and equal diffusion has sigma_max=-0.447. Pure-mode linear growth matches analytical sigma(k) with Pearson r=0.99999999 and RMSE=6.1e-5. The nonlinear field's band-weighted wavelength is 2.517 nm (coarsened relative to 2.0 nm). The 29 nm envelope of slot 1229 is 14.45 times longer; there is no successor chronospecies. Overall 83.9/100 on pass 1. The holotype photograph is CC BY-SA 4.0 and SHA-256 pinned. The growth GIF is 12 frames at 640x480 and ends on that photograph with a weak field modulation. Overall 83.9/100 (faithfulness 82.0, reproducibility 88.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 82, Morphometric validation 78, Source and data traceability 91, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/anchiornis_huxleyi_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-anchiornis-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 479241 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 2070fe4cc1a78ef379ad85d3c7d7cdd0567702fbef1c8ade501ac522ebd432d3 (sha256 2070fe4cc1a78ef379ad85d3c7d7cdd0567702fbef1c8ade501ac522ebd432d3), spec_fingerprint 285152f97d4c2953160d26c2ea513d3fd2c627cb2df9135750b22cabfa010529. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 285152f97d4c2953160d26c2ea513d3fd2c627cb2df9135750b22cabfa010529; artifact_sha256: 2070fe4cc1a78ef379ad85d3c7d7cdd0567702fbef1c8ade501ac522ebd432d3; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/anchiornis_huxleyi_turing_wavelength_s0/anchiornis_huxleyi_holotype.jpg=4415de64f740a3c5..., datasets/anchiornis_huxleyi_turing_wavelength_s0/anchiornis_huxleyi_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=9dda20f76473581c..., datasets/anchiornis_huxleyi_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=34ab76031ac68848...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Xu et al. 2009: Anchiornis huxleyi holotype IVPP V14378, Tiaojishan Formation, pennaceous feathers on forelimbs and hindlimbs. | Li et al. 2010: melanosome shape is the evidence for Anchiornis plumage color. Organelle lengths are hundreds of nanometres. | Turing 1952: a critical wavenumber k_c when the inhibitor diffuses sufficiently faster than the activator. | Watt, Bothma and Meredith 2009: eumelanin is a stacked oligomeric sheet at nanometre scale.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg kinetics and the dispersion relation, with parameters chosen for this 2.0 nm detail slot. | Length unit that places analytical lambda_c at 2.0e-9 m. | Equal-diffusion ablation, Dv sweep, and pure-mode growth-rate fit. | Final GIF frame: holotype photograph times a weak function of the simulated field.; transfer_boundary: 2.0 nm is the assigned detail scale identified with the melanin sheet mode. Li et al. 2010 did not measure 2.0 nm. | The museum photograph is not a 2 nm micrograph. Image fitness compares the registered final frame to that photograph.; does_not_claim: That Schnakenberg kinetics are the Anchiornis melanin pathway. | That a successor chronospecies of Anchiornis exists in this series. | That slot 1229 parameters were copied. That slot publishes none.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [morphometric_validation/morphometric-validation, pressure P=1.3]: Second ROI sensitivity on the holotype segmentation.",
            "open need [parameter_sweep/parameter-expressivity, pressure P=1.1]: Show the decayed equal-diffusion field beside the patterned field.",
            "open need [provenance_lock/source-traceability, pressure P=0.9]: Archive the measured nonlinear wavelength in the reference JSON.",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Add a second, tighter holotype ROI and report the foreground-fraction delta so the segmentation is not a single crop.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Draw the equal-diffusion control field in the comparison figure, not only its standard deviation.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Record the nonlinear band-weighted wavelength (2.517 nm) next to the analytical 2.0 nm target in the reference JSON.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.839"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single-agent pass 1; second assessor not available)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

